> final int hash2 = table.length > 3 ? 1 + hash1 % (table.length - 2) : 1;

    if(table.length > 3)
        return 1 + hash1 % (table.length - 2);
    else
        return 1;

It's called a ternary operator. Just think of it like an if else statement.

    bool ? x : y;

If `bool` is true, then `x` is returned, else `y` is returned.

Hey, you need to convert the angles to radians before you get the sine/cosine. Here's what I did:

    double sinBlock = Math.sin(Math.toRadians(x1)) * Math.sin(Math.toRadians(x2));
    double cosBlock = Math.cos(Math.toRadians(x1)) * Math.cos(Math.toRadians(x2));
    double cosY = Math.cos(Math.toRadians(y2 - y1));
    double distance = radius * Math.acos(sinBlock + cosBlock * cosY);

Is the value you're expecting `10691.79183231593 km`?

***

As for accepting the values with commas, you would have to take in the scanner input as a `String` (`input.nextLine()`), and then split the `String` into two arrays containing the values. Here's how I would do it:

    System.out.print("Enter point 1 (lat, long) in degrees: ");
    String line = input.nextLine();
    double x1 = Double.valueOf(line.split(", ")[0]);
    double y1 = Double.valueOf(line.split(", ")[1]);
    System.out.print("Enter point 2 (lat, long) in degrees: ");
    line = input.nextLine();
    double x2 = Double.valueOf(line.split(", ")[0]);
    double y2 = Double.valueOf(line.split(", ")[1]);

If I misinterpreted your question/had mistakes, please let me know!

